# Code efficiency (Terrana ERP)

Optimize for speed as modules grow. Prefer simple, measurable patterns over premature abstraction.

## Data fetching (Next.js + Supabase)

- Default list pages to **25 rows** with server-side pagination (`range` / `limit` + `offset` or cursor).
- Fetch only columns needed — never `select('*')` on large tables.
- Use **Server Components** for initial data; reserve `"use client"` for interactivity only.
- Parallelize independent queries with `Promise.all`; avoid sequential waterfalls in layouts.
- Cache stable reads with `unstable_cache` or route segment config where data is not user-specific.

## React & UI

- Keep client components small; lift data fetching to server when possible.
- Memoize only when profiling shows a problem — don't blanket `useMemo`/`useCallback`.
- Virtualize long lists (100+ rows) instead of rendering full tables.
- Debounce search/filter inputs (~300ms); don't query on every keystroke.

## Bundle & assets

- Dynamic-import heavy charts, PDF, or export libraries.
- Use `next/image` for photos; avoid large unoptimized assets in `public/`.

## Anti-patterns (avoid)

- Loading entire tables into memory for client-side filter/sort.
- N+1 queries (loop of Supabase calls — batch or join instead).
- Polling when Supabase realtime or revalidate-on-action is enough.
- Duplicating business logic in client and server — keep calculations server-side.

## When adding a feature

Ask: *Will this still be fast at 10× data?* If not, paginate, index (DB), or defer loading.
